2026-10-30T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2351) 'one ledger of BORING-TOKENs and INNOVATION-TOKENs for three orgs
 # uuid: c1f06557-6423-59af-b06b-c229bfc40a0f
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-10-30T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2351) 'a token is what the stack cannot run without: twenty, six INNOVATION-TOKENs and fourteen BORING-TOKENs
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2351) 'the token ledger in the private working agreements and the private plan, the private blocklist, and the repos of V-Sekai-fire, chibifire-stages and the private org
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2351) 'Which of the twenty tokens are INNOVATION-TOKENs, and which are BORING-TOKENs?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2351) 'The stack crashes without any of the twenty, and only six of them are new risk.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2351) 'Check a new technology against the rule: a token is a substrate, and the tech stack crashes without it. Write it BORING-TOKEN if its failures are widely known, INNOVATION-TOKEN if not.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2351) 'one ledger of BORING-TOKENs and INNOVATION-TOKENs for three orgs
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2351) 'A token is a substrate: delete it and the tech stack crashes. The name keeps it apart from a credential (operator, 2026-11-01). The ledger has twenty tokens. Each is a BORING-TOKEN, whose failures are widely known and which runs as shipped, or an INNOVATION-TOKEN, which is our own build, a fork or a use nobody has run. The INNOVATION-TOKENs are guest ELFs on the pinned double engine as row 1, which also runs the pen, `zone.elf`, the ggml-rd models, `slug.elf`, voice, the USD guest and the Lean tests, then SQLite on FoundationDB pages as row 2, FEX as row 6, the Fedora cross-build image as row 12, osxcross as row 15 and the taskweft persona engine as row 18. The BORING-TOKENs are Bao as row 3, our fork with an FDB storage backend, then Fly as row 4, which hosts the store, Bao and the KMS key that unseals Bao, then Tailscale as row 5, Proton as row 7, Windows as row 8, pixi as row 9, prek as row 10, GitHub as row 11, LLVM as row 13, llvm-mingw as row 14, SteamVR as row 16, Godot Engine as row 17, Elixir as row 19 and steamac as row 20. The operator ruled Elixir and Proton BORING-TOKENs on 2026-11-01, and Bao a BORING-TOKEN on 2026-11-12 although it is a fork. CockroachDB is retired (operator, 2026-10-18), and the guest BEAM is unship (operator, 2026-10-29). The count was three, then two INNOVATION-TOKENs, and is twenty tokens of which six are INNOVATION-TOKENs. The ledger changes between rungs, not in an open one, and the operator moved the two documents on 2026-10-30 rather than wait for a rung to claim them.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2351) 'The measured gap
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2351) 'The upstream orgs ran a second database. Of 312 repos that use a non-boring technology, 182 fit inside one INNOVATION-TOKEN when each technology is its own.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2351) 'How the ledger was found
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2351) 'The operator requested it on 2026-10-18: study the three orgs and consolidate the INNOVATION-TOKENS with frontier learning, with no limit on the count. Each org is a level. Each repo that uses a non-boring technology is a problem: 298 in V-Sekai-fire, 10 in the private org (the local checkouts, because the token cannot list the org) and 4 in chibifire-stages. A problem passes when every technology it uses is in one INNOVATION-TOKEN. Repos were tagged against 33 technologies from their names, descriptions, topics and languages.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2351) 'A step tries one move, "technology X rides on INNOVATION-TOKEN Y". The level with the most regret picks it. The move is kept only when total passes rise and at least two repos use both. Two planted moves with no relation (Ink onto OpenBao, Janet onto CockroachDB) were controls, and both were rejected.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2351) 'What it measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Passes rose from 182 to 263 of 312 (58% to 84%): 23 moves kept, 11 rejected.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Per level at the end: V-Sekai-fire 251 of 298, the private org 8 of 10, chibifire-stages 4 of 4.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Kept onto the guest INNOVATION-TOKEN: the pen, `zone.elf`, ggml-rd (and the Python reference models and Slang kernels behind it), MuJoCo, OpenUSD, voice, Rust guests, `slug.elf`, the double engine with xr-pilot and CineForm, and Lean as tests.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Kept onto the BEAM: taskweft, MCP, holographic reduced representations.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Not merged, for want of shared repos: CockroachDB, the casync chunk store, OpenBao and parquet into the store. Retiring CockroachDB was an operator decision, not a measured one.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2351) 'What is still split
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Elixir and guest code meet in 29 repos (taskweft compiled to a guest, the Godot build service, the MCP guest, the private org's double-engine repository). That boundary decides two big INNOVATION-TOKENS or one.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Terraform, Ink, Janet, TLA+, gaussian splats, hypercore and Go each sit alone. Each is a candidate to retire or park.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2351) '- The tagging reads metadata, not code. Two third-party engine scripting tags landed in the guest INNOVATION-TOKEN on a loose keyword. The moves were written by the agent. The measurement only checked them against shared repos.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2351) 'The parts added on 2026-11-01, classified
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2351) 'The operator asked for the ledger to name these parts and ruled that each is a token (operator, 2026-11-01). The class of each follows the test in the decision.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Row 3, Bao, is a BORING-TOKEN. The zone talks to the store directly, and reaches Bao rarely, to get or renew the credential it presents to the store.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Row 4, Fly, is a BORING-TOKEN. Delete it and the store, Bao and the KMS key that unseals Bao go with it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Row 5, Tailscale, is a BORING-TOKEN and is allowed (operator, 2026-11-12). The desk's Bao client reaches Bao over it (RFD66606-2399).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Row 20, steamac (github.com/fxgl/steamac), is a BORING-TOKEN (operator, 2026-11-12). It is third party. What it runs underneath, FEX and Proton among them, is not this ledger's.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Row 6, FEX, and row 7, Proton, are abandoned (RFD66606-2490, operator, 2026-11-12). The win64 build targets the Steam Frame and the Steam Deck natively.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Windows (row 8), pixi (9), prek (10) and GitHub (11) are BORING-TOKENs. The build and gate tools count as the tech stack.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2351) '- The Fedora cross-build image (row 12) and osxcross (row 15) are INNOVATION-TOKENs. LLVM (row 13) and llvm-mingw (row 14) are BORING-TOKENs. Each is its own substrate, so deleting one stops a cross-build.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2351) '- The SteamVR runtime (row 16) and Godot Engine (row 17) are BORING-TOKENs, and the taskweft persona engine (row 18) is an INNOVATION-TOKEN. Godot Engine and the pinned double engine of row 1 are separate tokens (operator, 2026-11-01).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Elixir (row 19) is a BORING-TOKEN (operator, 2026-11-01). It runs every gate and the ledger's own tools, and its failure stops them, so it counts under the tool ruling.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2351) '- GitHub's identity-token login rides row 3, because it is a login to Bao.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2351) 'What is not known
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2351) '- How many INNOVATION-TOKENs the stack may hold. The old limit was two, and six now stand.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2351) '- Whether the classes of the rows the operator did not rule on one by one stand as written.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

