 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2351) 'The BEAM row, unship (operator, 2026-10-29)
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2351) 'No guest runs BEAM bytecode, and no `beam.elf` exists in the tree. The only novel piece of the row is RFD66606-2330's static riscv64 BEAM, and that is the piece to unship. Counting the BEAM as an INNOVATION-TOKEN spent the slot that merging the pen and the shared world freed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2351) 'The two rows, moved (operator, 2026-10-30)
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2351) '- The private plan: "The three innovation tokens" is two. The ledger table's pen row and zones row are one guest row, which absorbs the "already paid" RISC-V row, and the store row is INNOVATION-TOKEN 2.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2351) '- The private working agreements: "There are three, and all three are spent" is two, naming guest ELFs on the pinned double engine as the INNOVATION-TOKEN the pen and `zone.elf` share.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2351) '- The operator moved both on 2026-10-30, outside a rung, rather than waiting for one to claim them, and RFD66606-2341's item left dev.next.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2351  1 LINE
 Text:Written

